    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d100-a1">

                <pb facs="0230" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg136"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No.
                        693.—Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Carazo to
                        Mr. Hall</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 26, 1887</date>.
                        (Received July 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the pleasure to inform you that in this moment the treaty has been signed
                    by which the question of boundaries, which has long existed between this
                    Republic and Costa Rica, is amicably settled.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Evaristo Carazo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
